Before the examination a student should be able to:
• identify the genre and form of an unfamiliar passage;
• analyse language without merely naming devices;
• explain structure;
• track character development;
• analyse narrative viewpoint;
• interpret dramatic stagecraft;
• compare two passages;
• construct a defensible thesis;
• use context selectively;
• evaluate alternative interpretations;
• write a conclusion that answers the question.

For every prescribed text create:
1. author and context;
2. plot in ten turning points;
3. character map;
4. theme map;
5. five important structural moments;
6. language patterns;
7. form and genre;
8. two or more plausible interpretations;
9. key scenes/passages;
10. ten possible essay questions.

Practice cycle:
Day 1: recall plot without the book.
Day 2: theme map.
Day 3: passage analysis.
Day 4: timed essay.
Day 5: rewrite weakest paragraph.
Day 6: comparison.
Day 7: closed-book self-test.

The aim is independent interpretation. Memorised “model essays” are less useful than a flexible evidence bank because examination questions vary.

EXTENDED STUDY COMPANION — Literature Revision Checklist and Exam Practice
Treat this topic as a network of knowledge rather than a definition list.

KNOWLEDGE
Know the terminology, procedure, text features and examination demand.

ANALYSIS
Ask how the writer's choices produce meaning. Move from evidence to method to effect to interpretation.

CONTEXT
Use context only where it explains a textual choice or a reader's possible response.

EVALUATION
Consider a competing reading and explain what evidence makes your judgement convincing.

COMPARISON
Compare form, structure, language, representation and context rather than only themes.

ZIMBABWEAN APPLICATION
Where appropriate, connect issues such as identity, gender, class, colonial history, migration, family, leadership and social justice to the text without pretending that all texts are specifically about Zimbabwe.

EXAMINATION
A complete answer should have a thesis, developed paragraphs, precise references and a conclusion. Never replace analysis with plot summary.
